<title>HONG KONG: HK Pacific Concord spinoff seen end October -- paper.</title>
<headline>HK Pacific Concord spinoff seen end October -- paper.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1996-10-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pacific Concord Holding Ltd is expected to raise HK$150-200 million by end of the month by spinning off its property division, Concord Land Development Co, the South China Morning Post said on Thursday.</p>
<p>About 80 percent of the new issue was expected for international placement with the rest for public offering, it quoted sources as saying.</p>
<p>Pricing would be fixed after meetings next week and listing of the shares in Hong Kong was seen by end-October, it added.</p>
<p>The company announced its spin off plan in early September but no detail was available.</p>
<p>Company officials could not be immediately contacted for comment.</p>
<p>-- HONG KONG NEWSROOM (852) 2843 6369</p>
</text>
